Dependencies that are not copied into this repository
=====================================================

Go modules
  server/ links the modules listed in server/go.mod and server/go.sum. They are
  fetched at build time and are not vendored here. Every one is under the MIT,
  BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause or Apache-2.0 licence; each module ships its own
  licence text (and, where it has one, its NOTICE), which a binary
  distribution must carry. `go-licenses report ./...` in server/ lists them.

Swift packages
  ios/HasalaCore/ depends on exactly two packages, pinned `exact:` in
  ios/HasalaCore/Package.swift and recorded in ios/HasalaCore/Package.resolved.
  They are fetched at build time and are not vendored here; each ships its own
  licence text, which a binary distribution must carry.

  GRDB.swift 7.11.1
    Copyright (C) 2015-2025 Gwendal Roué
    https://github.com/groue/GRDB.swift
    MIT License (LICENSES/MIT.txt)

  Swift Collections 1.7.2
    Copyright (c) Apple Inc. and the Swift project authors
    https://github.com/apple/swift-collections
    Apache License 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)

npm packages
  reference/ledgerd-client/ and reference/ledgerd-pwa/ declare their
  dependencies in their package.json and bun.lock files. They are installed at
  build time and are not vendored here.

  The website (web/) and its Lighthouse CI tooling (web/lighthouse/) do the
  same. The built site (web/dist, not committed) bundles code from three of
  them (vite comes in through astro) into the JavaScript it serves, all under
  the MIT License (LICENSES/MIT.txt):
    - astro (Copyright (c) 2021 Fred K. Schott), whose client router runs on
      every page; https://github.com/withastro/astro
    - vite (Copyright (c) 2019-present, VoidZero Inc. and Vite contributors),
      whose module-preload helper is bundled into the invite page's script;
      https://github.com/vitejs/vite
    - uqr (Copyright (c) Project Nayuki; Copyright (c) 2023 Anthony Fu), the
      QR code encoder on the invite page; https://github.com/unjs/uqr
  The site lists them, and Inter, with their licence texts at
  https://hasala.app/licenses (web/src/pages/licenses.astro, from
  web/src/data/licenses.ts).

What is not in this repository
==============================

- The ledgerd PWA's built bundle (server/internal/webui/dist) has been replaced
  by a placeholder page: Hasala's server does not serve that PWA, and the bundle
  carried fonts, a SQLite build and libraries this repository does not
  redistribute.
- dither-kit (reference/ledgerd-pwa/src/components/dither-kit), which was
  vendored without a licence, has been removed, as has the ledgerd mascot
  artwork (reference/ledgerd-pwa/public). reference/ledgerd-pwa is reference
  material for product logic only and no longer builds on its own.
